@@ -25,6 +25,27 @@ that doesn't start with `/`), or when it does not resolve to a value within `doc
 member, an out-of-bounds array index, or the `-` array index, which per the RFC never resolves to an
 element.
 
+### JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) — an
+array of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` or `test` operations — to a JSON document and
+returns the resulting document as a new value. It never mutates `document`, `patch`, or any value
+reachable from either.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+const document = { foo: 'bar' };
+
+applyPatch(document, [{ op: 'add', path: '/baz', value: 'qux' }]);
+// => { foo: 'bar', baz: 'qux' }, and `document` is unchanged
+```
+
+It throws when `patch` is not a syntactically valid JSON Patch document (for example, an unknown
+`op`, or an operation missing a required member), or when one of its operations fails — a `path` or
+`from` that doesn't resolve within the document, a `test` whose `value` doesn't match, or a `move`
+whose `from` is a proper prefix of its `path`.
+
 ## Development
 
 - `npm test` runs the test suite.
